# Live e2e (Playwright project `live`, e2e/live/*.spec.ts) — real dev backend + Wompi sandbox.
#
# Copy to `.env.e2e.local` (gitignored via `*.local`) and fill in. NEVER commit real values.
# The `live` project is opt-in: `npx playwright test --project=live` (a plain
# `npx playwright test` and CI never run it). Without E2E_USER_EMAIL / E2E_USER_PASSWORD every
# live test is skipped. Variables already exported in your shell win over this file.
#
# Steps to run:
#   1. Fill in `.env.e2e.local` (below).
#   2. Make sure the app under test points at the SAME dev API (VITE_API_URL). If Playwright starts
#      the dev server it inherits VITE_API_URL from this file; if you already have a server
#      running (port 5173 is reused!), start your own against dev on a free port and pass it:
#        VITE_API_URL=<dev api> npm run dev -- --port 5198
#        PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5198 npx playwright test --project=live
#
# Test account: a dedicated, non-admin user in the DEV pool. The tests never mutate its data
# (they don't complete a payment).
E2E_USER_EMAIL=<dev-test-user-email>
E2E_USER_PASSWORD=<dev-test-user-password>

# Base URL of the DEV API (same value the app uses). Used for the login call and to check that
# the app under test talks to that same backend.
VITE_API_URL=<https://dev-api-base-url>

# Wompi SANDBOX public key (pub_test_...). Needed by the "Pagar opens the real widget" test;
# without it that test is skipped.
VITE_WOMPI_PUBLIC_KEY=<pub_test_sandbox_public_key>
